<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Q4 - Responsive Typography</title>
<style>
body {
  font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
  margin: 0; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;
  height: 100vh; text-align: center; background: #eef2f3;
}
section { max-width: 600px; padding: 20px; }
h1 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); color: #222; }
p { font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem); line-height: 1.6; color: #555; }
@media (max-width: 700px) {
  p { line-height: 1.8; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<section>
  <h1>Responsive Typography Example</h1>
  <p>This text scales automatically using relative CSS units and the clamp() function. Resize the screen to see how font sizes and spacing adjust for readability.</p>
</section>
</body>
</html>
